    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0838" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.24/12–1444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-14T15:00:00-05:00">December 14,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2017. From Wiley.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d784-f1"/> Thank you for your 1373,
                    December 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="59" xml:id="d784-f2"/> I had not intended to
                    discuss matter until raised by Colombian Government. I regret that attitude of
                        OPD<anchor n="60" xml:id="d784-f3"/> of the War Department has apparently
                    made it necessary for the Colombian Government to turn to the Mexican Government
                    for equipment for the National Police. [Wiley.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d784-f1" n="58" xml:id="d784-f1-content">
                <p>John C. Wiley, Ambassador Designate to Colombia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d784-f2" n="59" xml:id="d784-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Department instructed that conversations be suspended on the
                    Colombian request for rifles (821.24/12–1344).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d784-f3" n="60" xml:id="d784-f3-content">
                <p>Operations Division.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
